  "description": "RAKPID crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4 c 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H122 Eu9 O42 2+,C10 H2 O10 W2 2-. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2E (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2B (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2G (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3E (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3G (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3B (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; W1 (W) has 0 O neighbors; Eu4? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors; Eu5? (Eu) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.700-5.261 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.08-169.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Eu9(acac)16(OH)10[W2(CO)10(μ-H)]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 10 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
